{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "id": "h200-attn-20261020-01",
      "criteria": {
        "credible_improvement_required": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Removing duplicate planner launches provides a credible critical-path mechanism. The proposal supplies a cheap membership and runner inspection before implementation, and compares sharing alone against existing same-type reuse. Exposed H200 planner time remains unknown; measuring it is an appropriate first falsification question."
        },
        "h200_applicability_and_correctness_required": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "The three-file Python patch provides a plausible SM90 port without requiring small TP-local head counts. Active runner dispatch and compatibility across groups remain unknown. The patch states \"FlashMLA checks only shapes\"; its cache key does not itself establish equal live lengths, masks or replay state. The proposed correctness checks appropriately target these unresolved invariants."
        },
        "discriminating_experiment": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The design includes eligible sharing opportunities, actual planner-launch counts, all-rank coverage, real rejection, held-out traffic, separate profiling and at least five alternating paired full-run blocks. It distinguishes an existing feature, incompatible groups and hidden planner work. Useful-effect thresholds, regression margins, coverage requirements and a maximum experiment budget remain unspecified."
        },
        "traceable_engineering_support": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Observed artifact: #58818 creates a per-pass dictionary and uses \"tile_sched = cross_group_cache.setdefault(\". Author report: \"Planner launches per decode step drop from 21 to 4.\" That report concerns H20 TP8/EP8 with synthetic acceptance. Transfer inference: compatible TP1 groups might benefit. Current H200 membership, launch reduction and serving effect size are unknown."
        },
        "practical_value_and_portfolio_coverage": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The presence check is inexpensive, the patch is small, and restoring per-group holders offers straightforward rollback. This complements the two indexer proposals and could affect primary-workload decode. Primary-workload benefit and its ceiling remain unknown. Full-node parameterized cost is appropriate."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "The installed holder-construction excerpt does not establish absence of cross-group sharing at its callers.",
        "Sharing by configuration key is insufficient unless live-value equivalence follows from verified builder invariants.",
        "The H20 launch counts and synthetic-acceptance setup cannot establish TP1 launch savings or real-rejection serving gains."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Retain as a deferred candidate. Before implementation, resolve runner dispatch and equivalent sharing at the pinned commits. Specify how compatibility is established without adding production device-to-host synchronization, and distinguish shared-holder uses from planner launches actually removed during graph replay. Freeze useful-effect margins, coverage requirements and stopping limits before future testing. Weighted score: 76/100; the unknown applicability gate prevents qualification."
    },
    {
      "id": "h200-attn-20261020-02",
      "criteria": {
        "credible_improvement_required": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Avoiding scores subsequently discarded by masking, and potentially avoiding intermediate K copies, provides a credible conditional mechanism. The proposal checks installed dispatch and cache eligibility first. Dense, gather-only and direct-only arms are strong comparators. H200 exposure is unknown; long-context evidence justifies investigation without establishing value for native 8K/1K traffic."
        },
        "h200_applicability_and_correctness_required": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "An explicit SM90 FP8 implementation path is proposed, preserving dense fallback and device-resident live inputs. Complete scoring and dispatch bodies are absent from the excerpts. Actual indexer layout, shapes, dependency compatibility and graph behavior remain unknown. Independent numerical, causal, remapping, replay and model-quality checks are appropriately scoped."
        },
        "discriminating_experiment": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Mutually exclusive arms, fixed selector backend, matched-input complete-path diagnostics and server-token TPOT distinguish copy savings, scoring savings and selection effects. The plan includes eligible-call denominators, prefix and acceptance attribution, five paired confirmation blocks and held-out mixed traffic. Gather-path activation under production graph settings and quantitative decision margins still need specification."
        },
        "traceable_engineering_support": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "Observed artifacts establish default-off flags and interface declarations; direct loads and replay behavior are primarily described in comments and author prose. #62000 reports \"11.6% slower\" for one request. #62463 states \"This is one A/B pair, not a confidence-interval result\" and reports a C4 throughput decline. These support the draft's cautious attribution, but the executable mechanism audit remains incomplete."
        },
        "practical_value_and_portfolio_coverage": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "Combining gather and direct scoring as competing arms avoids redundant selections. Dense fallback, early eligibility checks and explicit diagnostic-only promotion rules limit wasted work. Integration and numerical validation are substantial, while primary-workload benefit, H200 workspace effects and feasible long-context concurrency are unknown. Cost remains correctly parameterized."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "The supplied excerpts support an author-described design, not verification of the complete scoring, causal-bound or dispatch implementation.",
        "Static direct-path activation does not supply a qualified mixed-workload crossover policy; short-context safety must be demonstrated separately.",
        "The gather comparator may have different graph eligibility from direct scoring. A configured flag alone cannot establish a meaningful three-arm comparison.",
        "DeepGEMM #399 reports a scheduler boundary fault with \"16 sequences with next_n=6\". Whether its fix is present in the pinned dependency is unknown and relevant to the dense reference."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Retain as a deferred long-context candidate. Separate inspected flag/interface code from author-described kernel behavior. Require complete scoring and dispatch review, reconcile the MQA API changes described in #61149, and check #399 fix membership. Define graph eligibility for each arm without using FORCE as production policy. Freeze numerical tolerances, quality and latency margins, run budgets and long-context-only promotion rules. Weighted score: 72/100; the unknown applicability gate prevents qualification."
    },
    {
      "id": "h200-attn-20261020-03",
      "criteria": {
        "credible_improvement_required": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Replacing eligible selection calls with a potentially faster backend is a legitimate testable mechanism. The proposal checks existing dispatch and build support before porting, and compares against deployed auto plus the strongest eligible native configuration. FP32 speed advantage and exposed H200 selector time remain unknown; neither must be proven before the proposed screen."
        },
        "h200_applicability_and_correctness_required": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "The patch explicitly adds \"or current_platform.is_device_capability(90)\" and Hopper FP32 input validation. This provides a plausible port path while retaining separate sparse-scoring gates. Installed resolver behavior, SM90 extension build, actual input eligibility and complete fallback integration are unknown. The proposed tie, ordering, bounds, graph and quality checks address the relevant risks."
        },
        "discriminating_experiment": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Disjoint comparator calibration, unchanged dense scoring, complete-path timing and eligibility-stratified counters distinguish selector benefit from copies or changed semantics. Five alternating paired full-run blocks, held-out shapes and separate combination testing satisfy the principal design requirements. Concrete quality tolerances, useful-effect margins and stopping limits remain to be fixed."
        },
        "traceable_engineering_support": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Observed artifact: #59204 includes availability, dtype and alignment guards. Its page reports \"This pull request has merge conflicts\" but supplies no performance results. DeepSelect #14's performance claims concern H20 BF16; the competing radix comment's hardware, dtype and timing units are unknown. The draft correctly treats FP32 H200 gains as transfer inference."
        },
        "practical_value_and_portfolio_coverage": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "Build inspection and operator screening offer inexpensive falsification before serving confirmation. Rebase and extension compatibility add integration uncertainty. Selection is distinct from planner sharing, but candidate-only scoring changes its workload and may reduce its incremental value. Separate initial testing and non-additive combination claims are appropriate."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "The installed sparse-scoring helper's SM100 gate does not establish the installed standalone selector's dispatch.",
        "The BF16 cluster benchmark does not establish a faster FP32 path for this integration, especially on compact or higher-row-count inputs.",
        "Availability checks and an exported operator do not prove that the loaded extension contains compatible SM90 kernels.",
        "Rebase, build and resolver changes are only partially visible; their compatibility with the pinned serving branch remains unknown."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Retain as a deferred selector candidate. Specify the extension revision and SM90 build requirements, and resolve the complete installed resolver before choosing activation versus porting. State that the excerpt retains an existing end-bounded interface rather than demonstrating newly added bounded-row semantics. Freeze comparator calibration, quality margins and stopping limits; keep compact-logit combinations separate. Weighted score: 74/100; the unknown applicability gate prevents qualification."
    }
  ],
  "global_gaps": [
    "The rubric requests five selections, the brief count is four, and the draft contains three hypotheses. The portfolio is incomplete; each supplied hypothesis was reviewed exactly once without inventing additional selections.",
    "All three proposals provide credible mechanisms and cheap baseline checks. None has an established required-gate failure, but unresolved applicability prevents qualification regardless of weighted score. Missing H200 speedups are evidence gaps, not factual contradictions.",
    "Factual-support passes concern faithful reporting and attribution of supplied artifacts and author claims. They do not certify implementation correctness, author measurements or predicted transfer. No independent H200 performance results for these proposed changes are supplied.",
    "G01-G05 definitions, historical scorer implementation, production SLOs and full eight-GPU node price remain unknown. Before future execution, define acceptance margins, minimum opportunity coverage, numerical and quality tolerances, and bounded stopping rules without borrowing B200 prices or treating provisional diagnostic SLOs as production requirements.",
    "The repository list contains 16 names despite references to 13. Search records, title-only leads and patch metadata do not establish complete repository or implementation coverage. The rubric's statement that no implementation artifacts are supplied is stale relative to the included excerpts.",
    "Current attention and MoE dispatch, reported allgather_reducescatter configuration, harness compatibility and profiler readiness remain unverified. Runtime arguments attest configuration, not kernel activation.",
    "Small-head TP4/TP8 results do not establish a padding-removal benefit for TP1's 64 attention heads. MISA's supplied abstract and excerpt gaps provide no implementation or experimental support. Historical novelty rejections have no force under this rubric.",
    "No tools, file changes, agents or experiments were used. Describing later bounded GPU experiments is compatible with the research-session execution prohibition."
  ]
}
